==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Nosferatu Yukimura''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Vampiric Yukimura''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Count Yukimura's points of interest are basically the same as his original variant, Sanada Yukimura, which includes high speed, fast foreswing, high damage and sheer disposability for an Uber. He's best suited to either deal heavy damage to the enemy base or to slow down slow-attacking, slow-moving or long-ranged enemy units such as [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]], making him also good for cheesing strategies. This unit's usage is also similar to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and other rushers, so he can be used alongside them.

Count Yukimura's massive damage against Floating enemies can be helpful against the likes of [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and [[Gobble]] by being a reliable knockback pusher, as his foreswing allows him to get an easy hit on them, while his backswing prevents him from being hit by attacks after dealing damage as your other units catch up. Despite the wide availability of [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] specialists, he still has his place against those difficult to approach, such as [[Spacefish Jones]] and [[Cli-One]], given these openings do not persist for long and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] may not be able to catch up in time.

Additionally, his Survive ability could allow him to occasionally get one last hit off to enemies, and works better than usual due to his short cooldown. However, due to the fairly low chance, this should be treated a bonus, instead of being relied upon for him to survive engagements.

==='''True Form'''===
In [[True Form]], Vampiric Yukimura now always survives lethal strikes, with higher speed and damage. The former is perhaps the most important aspect, as while still unreliable, Yukimura's very short foreswing and extreme speed will usually guarantee one last hit, possibly turning a losing battle on its heel. Speaking of speed, Yukimura is able to reach distant targets more comfortably, all while hitting harder, so they shouldn't be overshadowed either.

